        שחקן העונה — why it moves
        ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        player            attended  gate?   stored avg   real avg   sentinel nights
        Linoy Levi           18     yes       6.000      7.114        9   (7 rated of 3 counted)
        איציק לוי            17     yes       6.000      6.870        5   (10 rated of 2 counted)
        מתן לוי              19     yes       6.000      6.640        6   (10 rated of 3 counted)
        Lioz Madar           18     yes       6.000      7.338        8   (8 rated of 3 counted)
        Eliran Tzabari       18     yes       6.000      6.750        7   (8 rated of 2 counted)
        Nofar Tzabari        18     yes       6.000      7.140        6   (10 rated of 3 counted)
        הלן צברי             18     yes       6.000      7.656        7   (9 rated of 3 counted)
      
        Why "rated" exceeds "counted" — the accumulator shipped late
        ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        The archive counted 2-3 evenings per player; the club has 16 with a
        stored rating, and every one of them belongs to season 1 (13 carry no
        seasonId at all, which means season 1, and 3 are stamped s1 — checked
        game by game).
      
        `eveningScoreSum/Count` began writing on 16.09.2026, the last two days
        of a season that started on 27.07. Everything before that has an
        eveningStandings row — written by an older path — and never reached the
        season accumulator at all. So the stored average is not a wrong average
        of the season; it is an average of its final 48 hours.
      
        And those final 48 hours are exactly the evenings that ran with no
        rotation: 16.09 and both of 17.09 recorded ZERO mini-games. Every score
        in the counted window is therefore the 6.0 sentinel, which is why all
        seven averages are exactly 6.000 and all seven share the title.
      
        The reconstruction uses the 16 stored ratings and keeps only those a
        player actually earned — present in a roundHistory teamA/teamB for that
        evening. It invents nothing: an evening with no stored rating stays
        absent rather than becoming a zero.
      
        Documents this migration would touch, if approved:
          seasonSummary/HhzIwmjMl1i5HSOGHt3p__s1   → awards (9 keys)
          seasonCards/HhzIwmjMl1i5HSOGHt3p__s1     → winners
          users/{uid}/seasonTitles/*               → add/remove per title moved
          communityPlayerStats/{gid}__{uid}        → eveningScoreSum/Count (7 rows)
        Nothing else. No game, no roster, no lifetime counter.
      ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

